From a52a12f19a4488cfe2e757155380b6e87090812a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gtguerreiro-max <295622337+gtguerreiro-max@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:02:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 51/51] xenos: texture layout and sampler fixes from Xenia
 canary

- A packed level 0 keeps the whole mip tail at base_address, whatever mip_address says, and a
  2x1 texture packs along X (ace153c, 344fca7).
- A 2D array's levels after the base align to four slices, a volume's depth shrinks with each
  level, and a packed 3D level's Z uses its own number (bc6b7a0); a packed level 0 is laid out
  at power-of-two height and depth (81e3dea).
- Tiled 3D bounds: the upper one is the highest block's end, found per 8-block run (c332733:
  the closed form missed a bank 0x800 past it), and the lower one starts at Y = 8 in odd groups
  of 4 slices, where the bank swap stores it first (c9c8e48). The test checks both against
  every block of a region.
- A nonzero minimum mip level is sampler state: a base page is dropped only when it is the mip
  page, and the base map of a texture with a base page samples level 0 (4a863a0: 534307E2).
- force_bc_w_to_max forces the border colour's alpha to 1 (d0dd989).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
